    "contract": {
        "name": "GroupTransactions",
        "desc": "Demonstrates two complementary ways to read sibling transactions from\nthe current atomic group:\n\n1. Index lookup (`gtxn.*Txn(index)`): a runtime assertion + typed view.\n   Fails the txn unless the transaction at `index` is of that type. Useful\n   when the shape can't be encoded in the ABI signature, and may assert\n   facts about transactions coming later in the group as well as before.\n\n2. Typed ABI argument: declare a `gtxn.*Txn` directly as a method\n   parameter. Transaction parameters are purely positional: they consume no\n   space in the application args array, and the router binds them to the\n   transactions immediately preceding this call, in declaration order,\n   asserting each one's type before the body runs.",
        "methods": [
            {
                "name": "expectPayment",
                "args": [
                    {
                        "type": "uint64",
                        "name": "expectedAmount"
                    }
                ],
                "readonly": false,
